 "claim": "Every four-place knot class that fails on small 4-regular systems builds a link, so it is NP-complete on 4-regular 4-uniform systems and its failures are coNP-complete to recognise. Classes 1, 2 and 5 have five-point link pieces; classes 4, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10 and 12 each have a three-point piece (three internal points on four lines, one port per line) accepting a relation of the twelve class, so replacing each line of the twelve class's link piece by such a piece (lifting) gives a link piece. A regularization for link pieces of any size (equality cycles of copies, free ports filling spares and absorbers) then maps every signed instance to a 4-regular 4-uniform system with the same satisfiability, and Schaefer's theorem applies. Checked: the realizations by enumeration, every lifted link's accepted relation by SAT, and the regularization end to end against a SAT solver for every class.",
 "kind": "proof",
